     BoxForm`ImageTag["Byte", ColorSpace -> "RGB", Interleaving -> True],
     Selectable->False],
    DefaultBaseStyle->"ImageGraphics",
    ImageSize->{408.6666666666657, Automatic},
    ImageSizeRaw->{252., 275.25},
    PlotRange->{{0, 252.}, {0, 275.25}}], "Text"]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->
  "17601ea4-4dcc-0043-a207-af315d5fff4e"],
 StyleBox["\nThe four-dimensional space is\ndescribed mathematically by two \
congruent\nparts or \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]sheets,\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] \
corresponding to u>0 and\nu <0, which are joined by a hyperplane r= 2m or\n\
u=0 in which g vanishes .2 We call such a con-\nnection between the two \
sheets a \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]bridge\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], which \
marketing departments now call a \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]wormhole\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote].\n\n",
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0]],
 StyleBox["THIS  WORK  IS PARTIALLY  BASED  ON :",
  FontSize->24,
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.8, 0.3, 0.8]],
